2531	// Flash-combine the per-split normalized partials into the final O/LSE.
2532	// The old kernel ran one WARP per (qidx,head) looping serially over splits, so for small
2533	// batch*heads only a few dozen warps were resident -> the cross-split reduce was DRAM-latency
2534	// starved (~40% of decode time, DRAM <2% on hd256). Here:
2535	//   * grid = (total_q*hq, NB): each (qidx,head) is split into NB ~64-elem HDV tiles -> NB x more
2536	//     resident blocks so the strided per-split O loads have enough warps to hide latency.
2537	//   * warp 0 builds the per-split softmax weights in smem (num_splits <= 64).
2538	//   * the split loop is unrolled x4 with 4 independent accumulators -> 4 O loads in flight/thread
2539	//     (memory-level parallelism), the real lever on a latency-bound reduce.
2540	constexpr int COMBINE_THREADS = 128;

